[1m[38;5;231mShould Sentry receive an account identifier for correlation?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mHashed username (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSend a client-side hash digest. Repeat failures from one account correlate; the vendor never holds a real [39m
     [38;5;246midentifier.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Raw username
     [38;5;246mMaximum debuggability — you can look up the exact account. Makes usernames personal data held by Sentry, with [39m
     [38;5;246mretention and deletion obligations.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m No user context at all
     [38;5;246mNothing identifying leaves the browser. Reports cannot be tied to an account or to each other.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Random per-session ID
     [38;5;246mCorrelates events within one session only. No cross-session pattern, no account linkage.[39m
